# Inertia.js Integration Patterns

## Controller Responses

Controllers should return Inertia responses as shown in [app/Http/Controllers/ClubController.php](mdc:app/Http/Controllers/ClubController.php):

```php
use Inertia\Inertia;
use Inertia\Response;

public function index(): Response
{
    return Inertia::render('Clubs/Index', [
        'clubs' => Club::all()
    ]);
}
```

## Frontend Setup

The Inertia setup is configured in [resources/js/app.ts](mdc:resources/js/app.ts):

- Inertia plugin for Vue 3
- Ziggy integration for Laravel routes
- Error handling and progress indicators

## Page Components

Page components should be in [resources/js/pages/](mdc:resources/js/pages/):

- Use Vue 3 Composition API with TypeScript
- Define props interfaces for Inertia data
- Handle form submissions with Inertia

## Shared Data

Use Inertia's shared data for global state as configured in [app/Http/Middleware/HandleInertiaRequests.php](mdc:app/Http/Middleware/HandleInertiaRequests.php):

- User authentication data
- Flash messages
- Global application state

## Form Handling

Forms should use Inertia for submissions:

- Use Inertia's form helpers
- Handle validation errors
- Implement proper loading states
- Use CSRF protection automatically

## Error Handling

Implement proper error handling:

- Use Inertia's error handling for frontend
- Display validation errors
- Handle server errors gracefully
- Implement proper error boundaries
